Git            -   Tracks changes you make to projects so you can return to older versions, or update newer versions at any time.
GitHub         -   A platform that allows you to collaborate on projects and share them with everyone.
Repository     -   The location of all of your files for the project that you're working on.
Pull request   -   Invites other users to review changes to branches of projects.
Merging        -   A user adding changes they made in a branch onto the final version of the project.
Issue          -   Helps you keep track of tasks you'll work on for projects.
Branches       -   Allow users to edit a section of a project that's separate from the final version.
Cloning        -   Allows a user to make changes to their project on a different device.
Forking        -   Similar to cloning, but used on another person's project instead of your own.

